    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** (85.52) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13) as our primary offensive anchors. **Yordan Alvarez** is in a prime position to capitalize on a favorable matchup against Young, benefiting from a high xwOBA and a strong SP skill projection that pushes him into elite territory. Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is our highest-upside play for stolen bases; he faces a slow delivery from Matthews, and despite a slight negative impact from \"Wind In,\" his dynamic platoon advantage and top-of-the-order status make him an essential start. **Junior Caminero** (70.19) and **Colt Keith** (69.64) round out our top-tier plays, both thriving against high-xERA starters, with **Junior Caminero** specifically buoyed by a significant dynamic platoon boost.\n\nWhile **Carson Benge** (51.46) nearly cracked the starting lineup, he was ultimately relegated to the bench in favor of more efficient, higher-ceiling options like **Lars Nootbaar**, whose park-adjusted projection narrowly edges him out. We are closely monitoring the risk profile for **Trea Turner** (56.61), as his score is tempered by a difficult matchup against an elite arm in McLean, compounded by a slight negative impact from the opposing catcher's pop time. Conversely, **Christian Yelich** (66.17) remains a high-confidence play; his score reflects not just his solid matchup against P\u00e9rez, but the valuable secondary category support he provides through his speed, bolstered by the high probability of a stolen base attempt against a pitcher with a slow delivery.",
